<%# The settings in a window over the current page, like Claude, ChatGPT or Notion (from 768 px: on a phone,
    the avatar opens the settings page). "Settings" in the account menu loads a section into the frame below,
    and settings_dialog_controller.js opens the window once it has arrived. The settings layout wraps its content
    in the same frame: links and forms of the settings stay in the window, and /settings/... stays a whole page.
    A native <dialog> opened with showModal: Escape closes it, the keyboard focus stays inside, the page behind
    is inert. A title bar across the window holds its name and the close cross; below it, the menu and the section.
    open:flex only: a display class on a closed <dialog> would show it.
    tabindex="-1": the controller focuses the window itself when it opens, not its first button (the close cross
    showed a focus ring at once; autofocus on the dialog was not applied by Chrome). Tab then reaches the cross.
    No outline on the window: its content has its own.
    data-turbo-prefetch="false": a link hovered in the window was prefetched with the header of the window, and Turbo
    reused that answer, laid out for the window, when the same address was then opened as a whole page %>
<dialog id="settings-dialog" aria-labelledby="settings-dialog-title" tabindex="-1" data-turbo-prefetch="false"
        class="m-auto h-[min(720px,calc(100dvh-4rem))] w-[min(960px,calc(100vw-4rem))] flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-0 text-ink shadow-2xl outline-none backdrop:bg-black/50 open:flex"
        data-controller="settings-dialog"
        data-action="turbo:frame-load->settings-dialog#open click->settings-dialog#closeOnBackdrop close->settings-dialog#closed turbo:before-cache@document->settings-dialog#close">
  <header class="flex h-14 shrink-0 items-center justify-between border-b border-line pr-3 pl-6">
    <h2 id="settings-dialog-title" class="text-base font-semibold text-ink"><%= t(".title") %></h2>
    <button type="button" class="<%= button_classes(:quiet, size: :compact_icon) %>"
            aria-label="<%= t(".close") %>" title="<%= t(".close") %>" data-action="settings-dialog#close">
      <%= render "shared/icons/x", css_class: "size-5" %>
    </button>
  </header>
  <%= turbo_frame_tag "settings_dialog", class: "block min-h-0 flex-1", data: { settings_dialog_target: "frame" } %>
</dialog>
